PATCH 389: fix the AZER2 (and other non-7a98/767c-path) mission crash -- FUN_0000_47e0's c68c=mga:0x2004
(cockpit-instrument bbox analyzer) dispatch passed its child/container args as RAW DGROUP near-offsets
(0x7ac0/0x7a42).  Patch 177 threaded them so while c68c was the uninstalled offset-0 no-op (harmless), but
patch 331 later installed DGROUP:0x68c=mga:0x2004 and patch 332 reconstructed 2004 to deref param_2/param_3
as HOST POINTERS.  On the AZER2 mission path 47e0's 3aa2-guarded c68c call fires (AZER1/CYPRUS1 instead reach
2004 via 7a98/767c -- patch 333 -- and set DAT_2000_3aa2 first, skipping this call), so 2004 wild-derefs the
raw offset 0x7a42 -> SIGSEGV (m_mga_FUN_0000_2004+0xc1, fault-addr 0x7a42; EBP chain e714->459a->206f->209e->
4846->4854->47e0->2004).  Rebase child/container to host ptrs EXACTLY like patch 333's 7a98/767c c68c calls
(al=0xff id, bx=0x7ac0 child->param_2, si=0x7a42 container->param_3, asm 0x47f9-0x4801).  Runtime-verified via
the FIST_SEGV_MGA diagnostic (commit b3ff8bc): word[DG:0x7a42]=0x55e9 (src seg), word[DG:0x1590]=0x4cf1
(scanline seg).  CALLER-side arg-thread (patch class 296/311/333), NOT a 2004 rebase (2004 is already correct).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
@@ -14135,9 +14135,15 @@
      descriptor at DGROUP:0x7a42 (its word0 = the off-screen fill-buffer segment that 2595 then fills). */
   ((void (*)(undefined2,undefined2,int))fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c560)))(8, 0x1c00, 0x7a42);
   if (DAT_2000_3aa2 == '\0') {
-    /* asm 0x47f9: `mov bx,0x7ac0 ; mov al,0xff ; mov si,0x7a42 ; lcall [0x68c]` -> c68c = MGAVIDEO
-       offset-0 no-op (`ret`); args (al=0xff, bx=0x7ac0, si=0x7a42) threaded faithfully but inert. */
-    ((void (*)(undefined2,undefined2,undefined2))fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c68c)))(0xff, 0x7ac0, 0x7a42);
+    /* PATCH 389: c68c=mga:0x2004 (cockpit-instrument bbox analyzer) is now LIVE -- patch 331 installs
+       DGROUP:0x68c=mga:0x2004 and patch 332 reconstructs 2004 to expect HOST-PTR param_2/param_3.  Patch 177
+       threaded these args as RAW DGROUP near-offsets (0x7ac0/0x7a42), harmless while c68c was the offset-0
+       no-op but now a WILD host-ptr deref on the AZER2 mission path (EBP chain e714->459a->206f->209e->4846->
+       4854->47e0->2004, SIGSEGV fault-addr 0x7a42).  Rebase child/container to host ptrs, EXACTLY like patch
+       333's 7a98/767c c68c calls.  asm 0x47f9-0x4801: al=0xff id, bx=0x7ac0 child(param_2), si=0x7a42
+       container(param_3).  AZER1/CYPRUS1 reach 2004 via 7a98/767c (patch 333) + set DAT_2000_3aa2 first, so
+       this 3aa2-guarded 47e0 call is AZER2-path-specific -> targeted, no menu/settings-flow effect. */
+    ((void (*)(uint,undefined2*,undefined2*))fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c68c)))(0xff, (undefined2*)(g_mem+0x1c000+0x7ac0), (undefined2*)(g_mem+0x1c000+0x7a42));
     FUN_0000_60d9();
     DAT_2000_3aa2 = -1;
   }
